{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Yitro rejoiced.</b> Targum Onkelos renders ״וַחְדִּי״. And one needs to know why the verse speaks Aramaic here and did not use the clear language, which is the holy tongue. And although the Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 32a) [it may be written] in seventy languages, nevertheless a thing declares its intent when it changes its language." "It appears that the verse informs us that from the abundance of joy his flesh became sharpened, for you will find that when a person experiences joy to a degree beyond what is normally conceived in ordinary perception, a sensation is produced in him through an alteration of his temperament, and sometimes he may faint and sometimes he may be in actual danger. See what I explained in Vayigash on the verse (Genesis 45:26) ״לֵאמֹר עוֹד יוֹסֵף חַי״. Now Yitro, although knowledge of the good tidings had already reached him beforehand, nevertheless when he heard the content of the miracle, and all the more so the pursuit of the [angel/messenger] after them as I explained on the verse (v. 8) ״וַיְסַפֵּר מֹשֶׁה״, and that HaShem delivered them — his flesh became sharpened. And this matter is perceived by every living person who can feel."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:32.479077839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}